From: Oliphaunt Maintainers <dev@oliphaunt.dev>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wasmer-js: copy direct protocol bytes through guest memory

Use the direct guest input/output exports with JavaScript typed arrays to
avoid redundant Rust staging. Returned protocol bytes remain owned copies;
no borrowed view may escape across guest reentry or memory growth. The copy
boundary is part of the downstream ABI and must remain independently safe.

